# Browser
# As a person sees it: Bot2's Lightstall Inquisitor asks Bot1 to exile a card from its hand, and the prompt says so. The
# Forest Bot1 exiles says over its art what the permission is and what it adds - for as long as it stays in exile, a spell
# cast this way costs {1} more and a land played this way enters tapped - and the Exile button is lit on Bot1's turn. Bot1
# clicks it open and plays the Forest from there, and it enters tapped (CR 614.1c).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Lightstall Inquisitor
Plains x15

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightstall Inquisitor.Cast
Bot2.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Lightstall Inquisitor: exile a card from your hand
Bot1.Choose(Forest)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Client.Bot1.Exile.Lit = true
? Client.Bot1.Exile.Forest.Annotation = Playable while it stays here, a spell costs {1} more, a land enters tapped
Bot1.Exile.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = true
